# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MOASYS-Vault — Audiobooks ignore list (EXAMPLE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A "do not warn me about this" list for your audiobooks library. Anything
# you put here gets silently dropped from
# output/<drive>/audiobooks/warnings.json on every run.
#
# Ignore lists are per DRIVE as well as per type, because the paths below are
# relative to that drive's root_path. `<drive>` is the lowercased `name` of a
# root in config.json — e.g. `server`, `external`.
#
# How to use this file:
#   1. Copy this file to `ignored/<drive>/audiobooks.yaml` (create the drive
#      folder, drop the `.example` suffix). The real per-drive files are
#      gitignored so your personal decisions don't end up in version control.
#   2. Add path prefixes below — one per line.
#   3. Re-run `npm run audiobooks <drive>`. Matching warnings disappear from
#      output.
#
# Two entry shapes — pick whichever fits each case:
#
#   # 1. Path-only (a bare string) — silences EVERY warning under this path.
#   - Audible/J.R.R. Tolkien/The Lord of the Rings
#
#   # 2. Type-scoped (an object) — silences only the listed warning types
#   #    under this path. Other warnings on the same path stay visible.
#   - path: Audible/J.R.R. Tolkien/The Lord of the Rings
#     types:
#       - warn_chapter_gaps
#
# Matching is case-insensitive and forward-slash-normalized, so the same
# file works on Windows (backslashes) and macOS/Linux (forward slashes).
#
# Get the paths to add from output/<drive>/audiobooks/warnings.json — paths live under
# each `by_type` bucket. Most audiobook warnings use a `<Category>/<Author>/<Book>`
# path shape (or `<Author>/<Book>` if you don't use category subfolders).
# The bucket key (e.g. `warn_duplicate_book`) is the warning type; you can
# also find every type listed in rules/audiobooks.yaml under `checks`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# Silence one book
# (Drops every warning under this book's folder. Useful for a book with
# known missing chapters or chapter naming you've decided to keep.)
# - J.R.R. Tolkien/The Lord of the Rings
# - Terry Pratchett/Discworld 41


# Silence a whole category folder
# (Drops EVERY warning under this folder.)
# - Other Audible
# - Book On CD


# Silence a whole author
# (Rare — usually only useful when one author's catalog has the same
# recurring issue across every book.)
# - Some Author


# Silence one warning type for a specific path
# (Most precise option. The example below silences ONLY chapter-gap warnings
# on a single book — everything else under it stays visible.)
# - path: Audible/J.R.R. Tolkien/The Lord of the Rings
#   types:
#     - warn_chapter_gaps
